      title="Dynamic vs Static Gas Pressure Testing"
      trade="Gas Appliance Commissioning"
      content="Never test gas pressure while the water heater is sitting idle (static pressure). Static pressure will often read a healthy 7.0 inches of water column even through a drinking straw. You must connect a digital manometer to the test port, turn on two hot showers so the tankless fires at 100% full modulation, and observe the dynamic operating pressure. If the reading plummets below 5.0 inches w.c. (or below 4.0 inches on some models), your pipe is undersized."
    />
  </div>

